<title>CANADA: TransCanada group wins Mexico pipeline.</title>
<headline>TransCanada group wins Mexico pipeline.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCanada PipeLines Ltd said on Thursday its consortium won a 26-year contract to build, own and operate a 700 km natural gas pipeline in Mexico's Yucatan peninsula.</p>
<p>Partners in the Merida pipeline project include TransCanada with 62.5 percent, International Generating Co (InterGen) with 32.5 per cent and Corporacion GUTSA with 5.0 percent.</p>
</text>
